On Nov 12, 2005, at 1:37 PM, Gabriel A. Devenyi wrote:

> Hey All,
>
> Just thought I'd point out a nice resource that I've used to put  
> together quite a few patches.
> The LinuxICC project (http://linuxicc.sf.net) builds the kernel  
> with Intel's C compiler and logs and
> categorizes some more useful warnings not present in GCC.

Very nice. Thanks!

>
> Also by the same developer, is LinuxCPD, the Linux copy and paste  
> detection program (http://linuxcpd.sf.net).
> He uses Red Hill consulting's Simian analyzer to locate copy+pasted  
> code in the kernel, which could be consolodated,
> or could contain errors without careful checking.
